---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '@/components/SectionHeading.astro';
const title = 'Privacy';
const description = 'This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. The application is local-first and shows you what leaves your machine before it leaves.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section padded="tight" class="pt-16 sm:pt-20">
    <SectionHeading level="h1" title="Nothing on this site watches you." lede="No cookies, no analytics, no trackers, no third-party scripts. The same posture carries into the application." />
  </Section>
  <Section rule padded="tight" class="pb-24">
    <div class="prose-site max-w-3xl text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="!mt-0">This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies are set and no local identifiers are created for tracking. The only stored value is your theme choice, kept in your browser's local storage if you change it.</li>
        <li>No analytics or advertising scripts are loaded. There is no fingerprinting.</li>
        <li>Fonts are served from this site's own origin. No request goes to a font network.</li>
        <li>The documentation search runs entirely in your browser over a static index.</li>
        <li>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log requests as described in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>. Vekrun does not receive those logs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If analytics are ever introduced, they will be lightweight and privacy-conscious, and this page will describe exactly what is collected before it is enabled.</p>

      <h2>The application</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>There is no Vekrun account and no Vekrun-hosted service your data passes through.</li>
        <li>Sessions, memories, indexes and task history are stored locally. You can delete them, and you can remove provider keys cleanly.</li>
        <li>Before anything is sent to a hosted model provider, an egress preview shows what leaves the machine. The first contact with a provider requires an explicit send.</li>
        <li>Telemetry is opt-in and off by default.</li>
        <li>Model providers you connect have their own privacy terms; what you send them is governed by those terms.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
